course: dictionary
lesson: 10611
title: Uneasy: the feeling that something is wrong
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Uneasy means worried, nervous or uncomfortable, as if something is wrong. «Alice starts to feel uneasy: what will happen to her when it's her turn to annoy the Queen?» Alice has not been hurt yet, but her feeling tells us that trouble may be coming.
explain: Uneasy can also describe a situation that is not settled. «An uneasy peace» means the fighting has stopped, but nobody is sure it will last. The meaning is not calm; it is tense and unsure.
explain: Your uneasy feeling can be a useful warning. If a person or place makes you feel uneasy, move away and tell a trusted adult. You do not need to wait until you are sure something is wrong.
fact: Uneasy means worried, nervous or uncomfortable, feeling that something is wrong.
fact: Uneasy also means not settled or likely to change, as in «an uneasy peace».
fact: Similar words are anxious and uncomfortable. Common phrases are «feel uneasy», «an uneasy silence» and «uneasy about».
fact: «A dog that yawns, licks its lips or looks away when the vet comes close is usually not tired but uneasy.» These are called calming signals.
fact: The «uh-oh» feeling is a warning. If it appears, move away and tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «Alice starts to feel uneasy.» What does uneasy mean here? | Sleepy and tired | Very happy and excited | *Worried, as if something is wrong | Fast and loud
exercise: A dog yawns, licks its lips and looks away when the vet comes close. What does this suggest? | The dog wants a big dinner | *The dog feels uneasy | The dog is very happy to see the vet | The dog is fast asleep
exercise: Which word means nearly the same as uneasy? | Sleepy | *Anxious | Cheerful | Generous
test: «The uneasy peace between the two villages lasted only a week.» What does uneasy mean in this sentence? | Calm and certain to last forever | *Not settled, so it might not change | Cheerful and friendly | Loud and busy
test: If a stranger makes you feel uneasy, what should you do? | Follow them to see where they go | Stay still and say nothing to anyone | Ignore the feeling because it is probably silly | *Move away and tell a trusted adult
exam: Which sentence uses uneasy to mean a feeling that something is wrong? | «The uneasy dog had a long, sunny walk.» | *«The stranger's stare made her feel uneasy, so she walked away.» | «The uneasy cake was tasty and warm.» | «The uneasy bus was painted bright blue.»
